{% comment %}
  UNWIRED from M&P card surfaces (Phase 13 round 3 — Dawn-native quick-add
  ruling, Nathan 2026-07-07): nothing fetches this section anymore —
  quick-add on cards is Dawn's machinery (snippets/hz-card-quick-add; Dawn's
  quick-add.js fetches the product URL itself). Stays in-repo as ported
  vocabulary (port-everything frame); re-wire = swap the gallery render back
  to snippets/quick-add. The Locksmith belt-and-braces gate below still
  guards the SRA exposure while the section exists.

  hz-quick-add-product — horizon-blocks Phase 13. The quick-add modal's
  content source, only ever rendered via the Section Rendering API
  (?section_id=hz-quick-add-product on a product URL — bare-filename SRA,
  section-rendering-product-card precedent). Two fetchers:
  - initial open: hz-quick-add.js fetchProductPage (its ONE deviation)
  - in-modal variant change: variant-picker.js SECTION_ID_MAP
    ('quick-add-dialog' → 'hz-quick-add-product', option_values=… params)
  Both extract/morph the <product-component data-product-grid-content>
  subtree; everything outside it (preamble renders, this comment) is
  discarded by the modal flow. ?variant= and option_values= pass through the
  SRA request, so selected_or_first_available_variant reflects them.

  AUTHORED section (not a stock-file port): Dawn-side stand-in for the shape
  stock's quick-add fetches off its OWN product page —
  snippets/product-information-content.liquid:97-121 (product-component +
  media + product-details) with blocks/_product-details.liquid:16-22 (the
  .view-product-title anchor + group wrapper). Our PDPs are Dawn-native, so
  that markup exists nowhere else; this section supplies the contract:
  - .product-information__media: MINIMAL media (plain flex column, first 4
    media via hz-product-media, preview-image-only; inline gap = stock's
    slideshow-slides --gap-2xs). Stock's {{ media_gallery }} (media-gallery/
    slideshow machinery) + its product-media-gallery-content-styles are
    TRIMMED — RE-ADD with the PDP media slice. Stock modal CSS styles the
    wrapper regardless; a media-less fragment would leave the mobile grid
    gap, hence minimal-media.
  - .product-details > group render whose children are the .view-product-title
    anchor (quick-add-dialog's #handleProductSelect updates this link) +
    STATIC blocks at schema defaults: product-title, price (emits
    <product-price>, required by the mobile re-parent), variant-picker,
    buy-buttons. The modal CSS allowlist (quick-add-modal-styles:434-477)
    hides everything else ≥750px; the mobile re-parent needs exactly
    .product-details / product-form-component / variant-picker /
    product-price / the payload attr — this set is complete.
  - view-event-payload via standard_event_data, stock-shaped.

  LOCKSMITH (belt-and-braces): this endpoint renders any product by handle
  OUTSIDE the gated card loops — the same lock gate used by the hz hosts
  runs first and empties the fragment for locked sessions (nil-safe: no
  product → nothing renders). Serve-probed for SRA leak.

  Host-page notes: the modal-content CSS ({% stylesheet %} aggregates) and
  element definitions must come from the HOST page — SRA fragments carry
  neither aggregate CSS nor executable scripts (morph doesn't run <script>).
  snippets/quick-add-modal.liquid (rendered by the gated hosts) eager-loads
  the JS; the hosts + card block render the style snippets. The preamble
  renders below are belt-and-braces for direct-fetch viewing and future
  non-host consumers, per the hz-blocks-host convention.

  disabled_on everything + no preset: never appears in the editor picker.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'component-group.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{% render 'hz-type-variables' %}
{% render 'hz-ui-tokens' %}

{%- liquid
  # Locksmith belt-and-braces gate (see header). Empty fragment when locked
  # or when fetched off a non-product URL.
  assign hz_qa_locked = false
  if product == blank
    assign hz_qa_locked = true
  else
    capture lock_content
      render 'locksmith-v2-lock-product' product: product
    endcapture
    assign lock_content = lock_content | strip
    if lock_content == 'true'
      assign hz_qa_locked = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- unless hz_qa_locked -%}
  {%- comment -%} --gap stands in for the PDP section's `--gap:
    {{ settings.gap }}px` (product-information-content.liquid:90; schema
    default 16) — the modal styles consume it for the sticky-bar fade masks
    and .product-details padding-block (quick-add-modal-styles:300/353/378);
    without it those go IACVT. {%- endcomment -%}
  <product-component
    class="product-grid"
    style="--gap: 16px;"
    data-product-grid-content
    {% # theme-check-disable UnknownFilter %}
    view-event-payload="{{ product | standard_event_data: 'view' | escape }}"
    {% # theme-check-enable UnknownFilter %}
  >
    {%- if product.media.size > 0 -%}
      <div
        class="product-information__media"
        data-testid="product-information-media"
        style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--gap-2xs);"
      >
        {%- for media in product.media limit: 4 -%}
          {% render 'hz-product-media',
            media: media,
            sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 384px, 100vw',
            loading: 'eager',
            preview_image_only: true
          %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div
      class="product-details"
      data-testid="product-information-details"
    >
      {% capture children %}
        <div class="view-product-title">
          <a
            href="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.url }}"
          >
            {{- product.title }}
          </a>
        </div>
        {% content_for 'block', type: 'product-title', id: 'title' %}
        {% content_for 'block', type: 'price', id: 'price' %}
        {% content_for 'block', type: 'variant-picker', id: 'variant-picker' %}
        {% content_for 'block', type: 'buy-buttons', id: 'buy-buttons' %}
      {% endcapture %}

      {%- comment -%} settings: this section's (empty) settings drop — every
        group-snippet read comes back nil, i.e. stock defaults (column
        layout, no background/link); the modal CSS overrides the layout
        anyway. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'group',
        children: children,
        settings: section.settings,
        shopify_attributes: ''
      %}
    </div>
  </product-component>
{%- endunless -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Quick add rendering",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["*"],
    "templates": ["*"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
